ntes</a> in the Santiago del Teide municipality on the west coast of Tenerife, Canary Islands. The species is endemic to the Canary Islands."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2012-12-15 18:48:32"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Cayambe\" title=\"User:Cayambe\">Cayambe</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":32934838,"title":"File:Eucera cinnamomea male 1.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Eucera_cinnamomea_male_1.jpg/960px-Eucera_cinnamomea_male_1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eucera_cinnamomea_male_1.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Eucera_cinnamomea\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Eucera cinnamomea\">Eucera cinnamomea</a></i> Alfken 1935, male sleeping on a capitulum of <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Carduus_argentatus\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Carduus argentatus\">Carduus argentatus</a></i>, Mount Carmel, Israel, April 14, 2013. Det. Stephan Risch 2014."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2013-04-14 07:54:22"},"Artist":{"value":"Gideon Pisanty (<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Gidip\" title=\"User:Gidip\">Gidip</a>) גדעון פיזנטי"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":76180603,"title":"File:Eugène Du Faget - Costume designs for Guillaume Tell - 1-3. Laure Cinti-Damoreau as Mathilde, Adolphe Nourrit as Arnold Melchtal, and Nicolas Levasseur as Walter Furst.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Eug%C3%A8ne_Du_Faget_-_Costume_designs_for_Guillaume_Tell_-_1-3._Laure_Cinti-Damoreau_as_Mathilde%2C_Adolphe_Nourrit_as_Arnold_Melchtal%2C_and_Nicolas_Levasseur_as_Walter_Furst.jpg/960px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eug%C3%A8ne_Du_Faget_-_Costume_designs_for_Guillaume_Tell_-_1-3._Laure_Cinti-Damoreau_as_Mathilde,_Adolphe_Nourrit_as_Arnold_Melchtal,_and_Nicolas_Levasseur_as_Walter_Furst.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Costume designs for the première of Rossini's <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Tell\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:William Tell\">William Tell</a></i>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laure_Cinti-Damoreau\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Laure Cinti-Damoreau\">Laure Cinti-Damoreau</a> as Mathilde <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolphe_Nourrit\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Adolphe Nourrit\">Adolphe Nourrit</a> as Arnold Melchtal, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Levasseur\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Nicolas Levasseur\">Nicolas Levasseur</a> as Walter Furst.\n</p>\nThe images quite obviously originally were meant to fit together.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The shadows stretch from one image to the other, and even the watercolour splotches and other minor elements of the painting match up perfectly. I presume it was cut up in order to send it to the various tailors who made the costumes, but it makes more sense as art put back together. Compare <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rossini_-_Le_comte_Ory_-_Eug%C3%A8ne_Du_Faget_-_Paris_1828_-_2._Le_gouverneur,_Levasseur,_le_comte_Ory,_Nourrit,_Ragonde,_Gosselin.jpg\" title=\"File:Rossini - Le comte Ory - Eugène Du Faget - Paris 1828 - 2. Le gouverneur, Levasseur, le comte Ory, Nourrit, Ragonde, Gosselin.jpg\">File:Rossini - Le comte Ory - Eugène Du Faget - Paris 1828 - 2. Le gouverneur, Levasseur, le comte Ory, Nourrit, Ragonde, Gosselin.jpg</a> or <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Costumes_-_Frederic_Lemaitre_as_Buridan,_Mlle_George_as_Marguerite_de_Bourgogne_(La_Tour_de_Nesle,_September_1832).jpg\" title=\"File:Costumes - Frederic Lemaitre as Buridan, Mlle George as Marguerite de Bourgogne (La Tour de Nesle, September 1832).jpg\">File:Costumes - Frederic Lemaitre as Buridan, Mlle George as Marguerite de Bourgogne (La Tour de Nesle, September 1832).jpg</a>"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1829"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Adam_Cuerden\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:User:Adam Cuerden\">Adam Cuerden</a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain"}}}]},{"pageid":76332521,"title":"File:Eugène Du Faget - Costume designs for Les Huguenots - 2. Julie Dorus-Gras as Marguerite, Adolphe Nourrit as Raoul, and Cornélie Falcon as Valentine.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Eug%C3%A8ne_Du_Faget_-_Costume_designs_for_Les_Huguenots_-_2._Julie_Dorus-Gras_as_Marguerite%2C_Adolphe_Nourrit_as_Raoul%2C_and_Corn%C3%A9lie_Falcon_as_Valentine.jpg/960px-Eug%C3%A8ne_Du_Faget_-_Costume_designs_for_Les_Huguenots_-_2._Julie_Dorus-Gras_as_Marguerite%2C_Adolphe_Nourrit_as_Raoul%2C_and_Corn%C3%A9lie_Falcon_as_Valentine.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eug%C3%A8ne_Du_Faget_-_Costume_designs_for_Les_Huguenots_-_2._Julie_Dorus-Gras_as_Marguerite,_Adolphe_Nourrit_as_Raoul,_and_Corn%C3%A9lie_Falcon_as_Valentine.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Costume designs for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giacomo_Meyerbeer\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Giacomo Meyerbeer\">Giacomo Meyerbeer</a>'s <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Huguenots\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Les Huguenots\">Les Huguenots</a></i>, No 2. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julie_Dorus-Gras\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Julie Dorus-Gras\">Julie Dorus-Gras</a> as Marguerite, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolphe_Nourrit\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Adolphe Nourrit\">Adolphe Nourrit</a> as Raoul, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corn%C3%A9lie_Falcon\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Cornélie Falcon\">Cornélie Falcon</a> as Valentine, for the Académie Royale de Musique-Le Peletier performance that opened 29 February 1836. Watercolour; probably 210 x 310 mm (Gallica lists ranges when multiple objects are in a set. The exact description is: \"aquarelle ; H. 120-210 x L. 080-310 mm - of which I'm presuming the smaller numbers refers to the single drawing. The crop is minimal.)"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1836"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Adam_Cuerden\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:User:Adam Cuerden\">Adam Cuerden</a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain"}}}]},{"pageid":79538701,"title":"File:Eugène Grasset - Jules Massenet - Werther.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Eug%C3%A8ne_Grasset_-_Jules_Massenet_-_Werther.jpg/960px-Eug%C3%A8ne_Grasset_-_Jules_Massenet_-_Werther.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eug%C3%A8ne_Grasset_-_Jules_Massenet_-_Werther.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Poster for the première of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jules_Massenet\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Jules Massenet\">Jules Massenet</a>'s <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werther_(opera)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Werther (opera)\">Werther</a></i>.  0,800 x 0,610 m"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1893"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Eug%C3%A8ne_Grasset\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Eugène Grasset\"><span title=\"French painter (1845-1917)\">Eugène Grasset</span></a></bdi> / <bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Adam_Cuerden\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:User:Adam Cuerden\">Adam Cuerden</a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain"}}}]},{"pageid":92954630